# S5-07 kernel stack-offset diagnostic N=2, 2026-11-16

## Question

The canonical `norandmaps` N=2 pair had identical 33-event `#PF` signatures, but its UART differed in three regions. In particular, the terminal panic unwind region contained 3 optional frames in run 0001 and 11 in run 0002. This diagnostic tests the same profile with Linux kernel stack-offset randomization disabled. It is a security-hardening intervention and is diagnostic-only.

## Command

```sh
target/release/od-runner linux-direct \
  --test-runs 2 \
  --series-id stage5-s5-07-kstack-offset-off-norandmaps-n2-20261116-a \
  --scenario-id stage4-init-nonce \
  --expected-stop-kind budget_exhausted \
  --out work/stage5/stage5-s5-07-kstack-offset-off-norandmaps-n2-20261116-a/series.json \
  --vmlinuz /Users/senya/projects/open_desktop/work/stage4/linux-7.0.0-38.38/vmlinuz-7.0.0-38-generic \
  --initramfs work/stage4/initramfs/initramfs.cpio \
  --acpi-blob tests/fixtures/guest/stage4/acpi_blob/stage4_acpi_blob.bin \
  --expected-vmlinuz-sha256 9f55ef7253055a9cf68f8a04323c93dead2fca617386d842fbde9ca7b178b27e \
  --expected-initramfs-sha256 65acac38cd4c791154f33179fe2c9f2103dd7fdec51aacfd969ab4d9eb0aedb7 \
  --expected-acpi-manifest-hash 2bd690ae0817705b1b128675f9628dd7212fee74ab97c88da3599a1ae8e398f2 \
  --ram-mib 128 --run --budget 3000000000 --set-cpl0 \
  --cpuid-profile stage4a --user-mode \
  --linux-norandmaps --linux-no-randomize-kstack-offset \
  --execution-observations
```

The release runner was built from codex commit `ab2f778`, which includes the reviewed diagnostic option from `b23fe6d`. Both runs used the same kernel, initramfs and 1104-byte CPU0 ACPI blob as the canonical `norandmaps` series:

